This handler was added so that support could diagnose production failures from a customer's screenshot.

```csharp
app.UseExceptionHandler(handler => handler.Run(async context =>
{
    var feature = context.Features.Get<IExceptionHandlerFeature>();
    await Results.Problem(
        title: feature?.Error.Message ?? "Error",
        detail: feature?.Error.ToString(),
        statusCode: 500)
        .ExecuteAsync(context);
}));
```

It uses `ProblemDetails` and a correct status code. What is wrong with it, and what should it do instead?

solution.code:
function statusForFailure(failure) {
  if (failure.kind === 'validation') {
    return 400;
  }
  if (failure.kind === 'unauthenticated') {
    return 401;
  }
  if (failure.kind === 'conflict') {
    return 409;
  }
  if (failure.kind === 'not-found') {
    return 404;
  }
  if (failure.kind === 'forbidden') {
    if (failure.ownedByCaller === true) {
      return 403;
    }
    return 404;
  }
  return 500;
}

